  "geometry_notes": [
    "45 mm top taper and 140 mm bottom taper are measured to the theoretical intersection with the web face (extension lines reach the web face on the 500 dpi render of SS107-16).",
    "R50 and R200 fillets are the unique circular arcs tangent to the two adjoining straight lines at each printed theoretical corner; tessellated with arc_segments chords (default 32; area error <0.008%, Ixx error <0.007% vs exact arcs).",
    "20 mm soffit chamfer taken as 20 x 20 mm at 45 degrees (convention; only '20mm CHAMFER' printed).",
    "Top-flange upper outer corners are square as drawn; no top chamfer called out.",
    "Web 160 mm (pretensioned standard). The guide mentions a 185 mm web for post-tensioned use; not a standard drawing, not implemented.",
    "Holes, dowel inserts, strands, reinforcement, end undercuts and bearing plates excluded.",
    "No published section-property table exists in any held Ontario source; checks are analytic only. The US Nebraska NU metric table does not apply (different outline)."
  ],
